{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>קרבם</b> — Some say it is inverted, קברם (their grave), and it is the house called בית עולמו. The meaning: they called their names after the buildings they built upon their graves. And some say the meaning of קרבם is as in וקרב איש במחשבתם (Numbers 16:28), that they stood firm in their hearts. In my opinion: it is defective of a bet, as if it were בקרבם (in their midst). The meaning: in the midst of the others who left them their wealth, and the meaning is that no memory of them remains except that one says, 'This is So-and-so's house,' and 'So-and-so built this tower.' And this is the meaning of קראו (they called [their names]), and all of this will not avail."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:16.664156221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}